A||||5||SCCA FIERO||Another headlight problem
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||05-30-99||06:54 PM||||Last week i was bragging to my Fiero buddies about how my headlights have always worked. I then showed them. Went up the first time and down. Then the second time the drivers side stayed down....DOH!!! Why couldn't this happen when i was alone?? Anyway i turned them off and raised it by hand. Then when it reached the top it decided to go down!!!   OUCH!!!! Freakin thumb went flying across the driveway(just kidding) It hurt like hell though. Now it won't even go down like that again. What could it be? I started looking through all the fixes on the web..nothing. I don't want to tear it apart until I isolate the problem.   86 SE V6
Z||000001||Bozone||05-30-99||08:28 PM||||Go to the Michigan Fiero Club's website. They have a whole how-to-fix-it complete with graphics that will show you all you need to know about Fiero headlights.
Z||000002||Gokart||05-31-99||04:54 AM||||I don't know how to actually fix that prob, but when I had an 85 a few years back, the drivers side headlight would not go down after being raised, so I got a extension cord and split it down into two, connected the two black connectors and the other end two the direct wires. Ran the end with the connecters inside the car by the hand brake. By connecting and unconnecting the black connectors I was able to raise and lower my headlight without spending a penny! Hack, maybe! But its something you could do before you may want to spend anything.
Z||000003||ChadMan||06-01-99||06:46 AM||||Gokart, you brought me some great memories.  I did the same thing with my dearly departed '84, except I used a momentary switch from Radio Shack mounted under the steering wheel.  This gave my Fiero the ability to "wink" at other drivers.  A cheap and fun solution!
Z||000004||Racer 1||06-02-99||11:52 AM||||When pontaic made the moters for the light they were high as kites.The grease gets hard inside and over time will wear down the gears inside I took mine apart and found the stock grease like rock hard!!! 8-(  anways I regreased them and they work fine! If your on a budget you could take out the motors and prop stick under the lights hehe!! Good luck
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||06-02-99||07:43 PM||||Well i thought maybe the relay was bad so i switched those. Still didnt work...checked all the wires/connections..looked fine. Did some stareing, swearing and got POed and whacked it. IT WORKED!! Then it stopped working.@#$@#$!!! I decided to pull it out. I took it apart and checked it out. The brushes were dirty and the com had crap all over it. I pulled the assembly out and gavi it a bath in cleaner. Installed everything(dropped a socket and had to pull it out again) and now it works fine!!!!! I wanted to regrease the gears but the case is rivited together. 
